  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner who completed a marathon in a bionic suit after being paralysed in a riding accident, has sadly passed away at the age of 44. She raised nearly £1m for charity, participating in events across the country. Claire became paralysed from the chest down in 2007 after an accident at the Osberton Horse Trials. Despite her injuries, she made headlines for running the 2012 London Marathon in a bionic suit over 17 days. In 2016, she completed the Great North Run while pregnant in her bionic suit. Claire was chosen to light the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square in 2012. Her family has asked for privacy to grieve her loss."
}
```

